core_rtl:
contains the RTL of the core with AXI4 master interface.

acu.v, arithbox.v, datacache.v, realign.v, shiftbox.v, synthetic_op.v are
hand-written behavioral RTL sub-blocks (address calc, ALU, cache array,
unaligned-access realign, shift/rotate, microcoded ops).

The rest of the core (bus interface, TLBs, instruction decoder, execution
datapath, microsequencer, and the top-level integration) is delivered as a
gate-level netlist -- previously a single 74k-line core_rtl/v586.v, now
split by module for navigability into:

  v586_biu32_axi.v  - AXI4 bus interface unit                (module biu32_axi)
  v586_dtlb.v       - data TLB                                (module Dtlb)
  v586_itlb.v       - instruction TLB                         (module Itlb)
  v586_decode.v     - instruction decoder                     (module deco + helpers)
  v586_vliw.v       - execution datapath                      (module vliw)
  v586_cpu.v        - decoder/datapath wrapper                (module cpu)
  v586_useq.v       - microsequencer                          (module useq)
  v586_core.v       - integrates TLBs/useq/cpu                (module core)
  v586_top.v        - top-level AXI4-wrapped core             (module v586)

Instantiation hierarchy: v586 -> { biu32_axi, core -> { Dtlb, Itlb, useq, cpu -> { vliw, deco } } }.
Each file's own header comment describes its role in more detail. Content
below each module's port list is a synthesized netlist of the notech_*
cells (see gate_rtl/) -- this split is purely organizational (verified
byte-for-byte identical to the original v586.v); no gate-level logic has
been rewritten. Reconstructing readable behavioral RTL for these blocks
would require genuine reverse-engineering of the netlist, which is future
work, not yet done.

soc_rtl:
contains peripherals for soc demo, mainly interrupt/timers/uart and spi interface

doc:
useful documentation

gate_rtl:
basic blocks used in some core or soc rtl

board_specific_files:
Will contain different top RTL for various board and
also the XCI files to generate the xilinx IPs like the AXI4 interconnect.
It will contain files for memory interface MIG DDDR2/3 or PSRAM rtl interfaces
for each board.
